  "changes": [
    "Telephone worker requires a validated declared manifest before recovery/claims, has one with_driver composition and always applies normalized start/status/end receipts; removed optional manifest/normalized flag/with_observed_driver/raw dispatch branch.",
    "Required adapter normalizer and manifest replace permissive defaults. Logical IDs are bounded before transport. Decoder failure after possible start/end/status transport becomes uncertain, including a local decoder rejection. Restart never redials an uncertain start.",
    "Read-only inbound discovery returns InboundVoiceReceipt with external call data, normalized voice state, stable event ID and reconciliation provenance. It has no local logical mutation ID; the authorized Store import mints and binds that ID inside its transaction.",
    "Inbound import rejects local-attempt provenance, mismatched carrier/typed state and invalid event IDs. Current ingress credential/route/assistant/phone/caller/time/conversation checks precede duplicate handling. Projection, local call and journal commit together. Projection storage failure rolls back the whole import; retry creates one call.",
    "Discovery decoder failure preserves scan cursor without importing or dialing. Repeated terminal inbound discovery and worker restart produce one typed terminal call and zero outbound starts. Existing status polling owns later updates.",
    "Updated connector contract and affected fixture implementations. Raw transport methods remain adapter primitives, not an alternate worker dispatch. No retired public call API was restored."
  ],
